WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.984
When Dugu Qieluo married Yang Jian, the two of them were both still very young.

00:00:04.334 --> 00:00:08.462
They promised to support each other for their whole lives.

00:00:08.812 --> 00:00:13.540
After Yang Jian founded the Sui dynasty, Dugu Qieluo became empress.

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:18.138
She wore splendid ceremonial robes, with an extraordinary bearing.

00:00:18.488 --> 00:00:23.000
She was clever and decisive, and often took part in discussions of the great affairs of the court.

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:26.590
The ministers all admired her insight.

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:30.540
Emperor Wen of Sui trusted her deeply, and their affection for each other was profound.

00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:34.802
They often walked together, discussing the affairs of state.

00:00:35.152 --> 00:00:41.632
At the time, people praised them as the Two Sages — an emperor and empress governing the country together.

00:00:41.982 --> 00:00:45.966
Such an imperial couple was rarely seen in history.

00:00:46.316 --> 00:00:51.956
Empress Dugu was one of the most important political figures of the early Sui dynasty.

00:00:52.306 --> 00:00:55.954
Her story is still told and praised to this day.

